 "assigned_role": "electrical",
 "description": "Moving to alkaline cells raises the pack voltage from 7.2 V to 9 V. The firmware motor output, which the pack constrains, keeps the base pwm_duty_limit of 0.833 (6 V / 7.2 V) with no reason given; it should be 0.667 (6 V / 9 V). At 0.833 the 6 V gearmotors see an average of 7.5 V, 25 % over their rating, and the drivers' 1.00 A pack-side current no longer follows from the duty the firmware allows.",
 "edge": {
  "source": "electrical.battery_pack",
  "target": "firmware.motor_output"
 },
